\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So, let's just consider the range of things that entered into the actor's
 and firm's utility and output.
 x, y, time and some generic factor1.
 y has yet to be defined.
 In some model runs, I'm going to want y to be factor1 - that is, for firm
 x to be using y as an intermediary (and perhaps vice versa - cf.
 Krugman.)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However, we also want space costs to enter into things.
 They can do this in a number of ways.
 
\end_layout

